      "extract": "Preface It is undeniable that geometric ideas have been very important to the foundations of modern discrete optimization. The inﬂuence that geometric algorithms have in opti- mization was elegantly demonstrated in the, now classic, book Geometric Algorithms and Combinatorial Optimization [145] written more than 25 years ago by M. Grötschel, L. Lovász, and A. Schrijver. There, in a masterful way, we were introduced",
